From d4c5f042fdcfcf62b247a6dc9c0aa679ce97e6de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicola Fiorillo <nicfio@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 21:36:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] media: ipu-bridge: Add GalaxyCore GC5035 and GC8034

NON INVIABILE: manca il Signed-off-by.

Both link frequencies were measured on a CHUWI Hi10 X1 rather than
taken from vendor code, which declares 438 MHz for the GC5035 and
336 MHz for the GC8034 and is wrong on both counts. Deriving them from
the frame rate gives 422.4 MHz and 268.8 MHz, which are 19.2 MHz times
22 and 14, the external clock this platform provides. The two sensor
drivers derive the same values from the clock at probe time, so the
numbers here and there have to be changed together.

Verificato che l'SSDB di questa macchina NON contiene la link
frequency: il campo maxlanespeed non viene popolato dal BIOS e resta a
zero, coerentemente con il commento in testa alla tabella.

Signed-off-by: Nicola Fiorillo <nicfio@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
index 88581a4c0..3047abd41 100644
--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
@@ -49,6 +49,10 @@
  * Please keep the list sorted by ACPI HID.
  */
 static const struct ipu_sensor_config ipu_supported_sensors[] = {
+	/* GalaxyCore GC5035 */
+	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("GCTI5035", 1, 422400000),
+	/* GalaxyCore GC8034 */
+	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("GCTI8034", 1, 268800000),
 	/* Himax HM11B1 */
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("HIMX11B1", 1, 384000000),
 	/* Himax HM2170 */
-- 
